{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384426-simplle-take-on-resonance","id":1384426,"title":"Simplle take on Resonance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-28T09:27:14-07:00","id":1384426,"title":"Simplle take on Resonance","content":"Resonance is a tricky subject, and the definitions between editions often contradict each other. M20 discusses this, and between the core RAW and Book of Shadows, the game attempts to simplify the situation by making things more complex. Not that I mind. I like options. Sifting through these options, I have come up with my own idea that I think is simple and sweet.<br /> Every starting character picks a Resonance Trait. No score, just you either have the trait or you don't. For each additional point of Avatar (I am starting everyone at a base of 1), the character may gain an additional Resonance Trait. What this is and the details can be worked out metagame between player and GM. But in-game the character has no choice.<br /> All the Trait does is qualify one for the -1 Difficulty modifier if they have an Appropriate Trait, and a +1 penalty for an Opposed trait.<br /> And that's it. Nothing more than that.<br /> My sistuation is that I am starting up an M20 game with a bunch of veteran Mage players that have not yet seen M20 or any current edition books. They have been operating with a mix of 2e and Revised. And, llike many Mage games, they just gloss overthe subject of Resonance (or just use Echoes).<br /> <br /> What do you guys think? Simple? Too simple? Not simplel enough?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T13:55:49-07:00","id":1384497,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I'd link it to Avatar. It forces high level Avatars to be thematically complex entities that can support that many distinct resonance traits. It also messes with the idea that the mage has the Resonance Trait if it's linked to Avatar.<br /> <br /> It might be better to do half of Arete rounded up to avoid contrasting with the role of Avatar beyond it's direct effect on your Quintessence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T14:57:06-07:00","id":1384516,"title":"","content":"my original thought was linking it to Arete, a mage would have a number of taits equal to one third Avatar (round up). So you start with one, and gain others at Arete 4, 7, and 10.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25651-marko-markoko","name":"Marko Markoko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25651_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}